This file lists the third-party software that sandboxd's release binaries
contain, and the third-party software that the scripts in this repository
download. Downloaded software is not stored in this repository: the scripts
fetch it at a pinned version and check its SHA-256 (or pull a base image by
digest). Each component keeps its own license.


Compiled into the release binaries
----------------------------------

sandboxd, sandboxd-pf-helper and sandboxd-guest-agent are Go programs.
Besides the Go standard library and runtime (BSD-3-Clause, The Go Authors),
sandboxd links the modules below; sandboxd-guest-agent links only
golang.org/x/sys, and sandboxd-pf-helper none. Versions are from go.mod;
each module's license files are in its source at that version.

- golang.org/x/sys v0.42.0: BSD-3-Clause, The Go Authors
- modernc.org/sqlite v1.50.1: BSD-3-Clause, The Sqlite Authors. It is
  translated from SQLite, which is in the public domain (SQLITE-LICENSE).
- modernc.org/libc v1.72.3: BSD-3-Clause, The Libc Authors. Its
  LICENSE-3RD-PARTY.md lists code from Go (BSD-3-Clause), musl libc (MIT),
  go-netdb (MIT) and NixOS/nixpkgs (MIT).
- modernc.org/mathutil v1.7.1, modernc.org/memory v1.11.0: BSD-3-Clause
  (memory also carries LICENSE-GO, LICENSE-LOGO and LICENSE-MMAP-GO)
- github.com/google/uuid v1.6.0: BSD-3-Clause, Google Inc.
- github.com/remyoudompheng/bigfft v0.0.0-20230129092748-24d4a6f8daec:
  BSD-3-Clause, The Go Authors
- github.com/dustin/go-humanize v1.0.1: MIT, Dustin Sallings


Downloaded by images/linux-amd64-fc/install-firecracker.sh
----------------------------------------------------------

- Firecracker and jailer v1.17.0 (x86_64 release tarball from
  github.com/firecracker-microvm/firecracker): Apache-2.0, Amazon.com, Inc.
  or its affiliates. Firecracker's NOTICE adds: portions Copyright 2017 The
  Chromium OS Authors, under a BSD-style license (its THIRD-PARTY file), and
  the release bundle includes libseccomp (LGPL-2.1), used at build time.
  The tarball carries LICENSE, NOTICE and THIRD-PARTY; the script installs
  only the firecracker and jailer binaries.
- Guest kernel vmlinux-6.1.186, built by Firecracker's CI (https://
  s3.amazonaws.com/spec.ccfc.min/firecracker-ci/20260930-a738f18a8db0-0/
  x86_64/vmlinux-6.1.186): the Linux kernel, GPL-2.0 WITH Linux-syscall-note.


Downloaded by the image builds (images/*)
-----------------------------------------

- E2B envd 0.9.0 (images/e2b-amd64-fc, images/e2b-arm64,
  images/code-interpreter-amd64-fc; also conformance/run.py): Apache-2.0,
  Copyright 2023 FoundryLabs, Inc. Release binary built from
  github.com/e2b-dev/infra commit 0c2108b1b76a66d18cf095d51fd7c51c703648ae
  (packages/envd). The images carry its LICENSE and a SOURCE note in
  /usr/share/doc/envd/.
- E2B code-interpreter template @e2b/code-interpreter-template@0.4.6
  (images/code-interpreter-amd64-fc): github.com/e2b-dev/code-interpreter
  commit 8d51873ccf620498347210dc3ec9698cf67c2829, Apache-2.0. This includes
  the code-interpreter server (template/server). The image carries its
  LICENSE and a SOURCE note in /usr/share/doc/code-interpreter/.
- Jupyter kernels in the code-interpreter image: IJava 1.3.0 (MIT, Spencer
  Park), e2b-dev/ijavascript commit 79cb7d56dcfe0df9ff55eff0ca4dc920a6dcc361
  (BSD-3-Clause, Nicolas Riesco and others), bash_kernel 0.10.0
  (BSD-3-Clause, Thomas Kluyver and contributors) and IRkernel 1.3.2 (MIT,
  IRkernel authors). The image also contains OpenJDK 11 (GPL-2.0 with the
  Classpath Exception), Node.js 20 from deb.nodesource.com (MIT), R from
  Debian, and the Python packages of the template's requirements files, each
  under its own license.
- Base images, pulled by digest: debian:bookworm-slim, golang:1.26.4-bookworm
  and python:3.13. Their Debian packages keep their own licenses; each
  image has the copyright files in /usr/share/doc/<package>/copyright.
- Go module caches of the review images (GOMOD_REPOS in
  images/linux-amd64-fc/Dockerfile and images/linux-arm64/Dockerfile): the
  module graphs of the listed repositories, each module under its own
  license.


Downloaded only by the conformance harness (conformance/run.py)
---------------------------------------------------------------

The harness runs, without redistributing them, the upstream test suites of
github.com/e2b-dev/E2B at the commits pinned in conformance/run.py
(Apache-2.0), the stock E2B SDKs and their dependencies from PyPI and npm
(conformance/python/requirements.txt, conformance/js/package-lock.json),
and the pinned github.com/gitmoot/gitmoot package, each under its own
license.
